0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186119715 1071 "![](images/95/95e3f2da04e23c9b42ea04cba3ee1d7cc069fef992592f09a70cef367b670f0d.png)\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: v, \\: u^3-v \\big\\rangle$ for $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 2.$ What is the missing expression?" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186119715 1071 "$AAAAAAAA$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: v, \\: u^3-v \\big\\rangle$ for $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 2$. What is the missing expression?" 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186119715 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D$, the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D \\left\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\| \\text{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\