](images/ee/eebd5724c98ea00681ef901dabae1d0b3428aff0c6e6a9cdadc020ed46f129c7.png) is \n![](images/02/0285f4ab3e7a9c974f244d0ab517ca737d2a5aec35bfbceb779037d54ce00f98.png)\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n![](images/d3/d3089c43ce61bf64a57a6d64b38987b91a6c8f9aa9f06d106f4c124ed430dd09.png)\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the ![](images/23/235efd30dbd8ca8883230793c8b79882afd19443c612b54f30b5cd507a646c9c.png)-axis is\n\n![](images/14/148b58f76868ac2f7a85e68627f91f2fa47c6c6a2bd5bcb67af8ba8af011167a.png)" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186129036 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$, we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n$I_x = \\iint\\limits_D y^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A$.\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n$I_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A$.\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n$I_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2+y^2) \\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A = I_x + I_y$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2-x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/68/68904cbee1839a61f4d65c5ff03066d8f28b8a5e070f6ddb00c82c29cfd93fcd.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac12 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = 2\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{M}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{x} &= ∬_(D)y^{2}λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{2}\\int_{0}^{2}\\int_{0}^{2 - x}y^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{2}\\int_{0}^{2}[\\int_{0}^{2 - x}y^{2}dy]dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{2}\\int_{0}^{2}[\\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{y = 0}^{y = 2 - x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{6}\\int_{0}^{2}(2 - x)^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{6}[- \\frac{1}{4}(2 - x)^{4}]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{M}{24}[(2 - x)^{4}]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{M}{24}(0^{4} - 2^{4}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{M}{24} \\cdot (-16) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186129037 1071 "![](images/46/46d6a57700d1df7f2de9a46507821a8553876eb956be6ef87a455d5ca0fabafb.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curves $y=x^2$ and $y=1$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. If the mass density function of $D$ is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 4xy$, find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis." 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186129037 1071 "![](images/46/46d6a57700d1df7f2de9a46507821a8553876eb956be6ef87a455d5ca0fabafb.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curves $y=x^2$ and $y=1$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. If the mass density function of $D$ is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 4xy,$ find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis." 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186129037 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$, we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n$I_x = \\iint\\limits_D y^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A$.\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n$I_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A$.\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n$I_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2+y^2) \\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A = I_x + I_y$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: x^2 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/88/8846da0fe3b1e8369a9277bbaba1e082d040136a71105a5816af7b13d2788027.png)\n\nUsing the formula for $I_x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{x} &= ∬_(D)y^{2}λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{x^{2}}^{1}