inally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](images/17/17dd9e10234b6a69123241a882e267d95d505d1944d7c31ef563f9ac06b990af.png)" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186133669 1071 "Consider the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $\\Vert A\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186133669 1071 "Consider the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $\\Vert A\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert.$\n![](images/82/8200befaaea3a0cdec7e423999839c72d48fc67110fa577c8707e182c4524aff.png)" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186133669 1074 "First of all, we write the given system in the form\n\n$$\nA \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(A)\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(x) &= \\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(b) \\\\\nAx &= b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by $A^T$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{T}Ax^(^) &= A^{T}b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix $A^T \\! A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $(A^T \\! A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(^) &= (A^{T}A)^{-1}A^{T}b \\\\\n&= (\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix})^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $\\Vert A\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert$ is attained when\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}={\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}\n$$\n\nwhich is the least-squares solution of the system\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{b}$ onto the column space of $A$, and $\\Vert A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert$ is the distance between the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ and the column space.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAx^(^) - b &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}22 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\Vert A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}-\\mathbf{b}\\Vert =\\sqrt{(-12)^2+0^2+(-12)^2+0^2}=12\\sqrt{2}\n$$" 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186133669 1074 "First of all, we write the given system in the form $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equa