t{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}.\n$$" 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186198245 1071 "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$. Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." 13194139533390 17592186045585 false] [17592186198245 1071 "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." 13194139533390 17592186045585 true] [17592186198245 1074 "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c)$, where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](images/a7/a7992c54f85f85cab3d9f923b8daca62c410393b364d30bcfbf5cff5efc93bbd.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{c} &= \\frac{1}{A_{D}}∬_(D)xdA \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}\\int_{-1}^{1}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}xdxdy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}\\int_{-1}^{1}[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = \\s